<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Quantum HTML + CSS example 08_typography/15: Styling the first line -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Styling the first line</title>
  <style>
    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif;
      line-height: 1.5;
      color: #1f2933;
      background: #f5f7fa;
    }
    .demo { max-width: 60rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; }
    .demo > h1 { margin: 0 0 0.25rem; font-size: 2rem; }
    .lead { margin: 0 0 2rem; color: #52606d; }

    .intro { max-width: 36rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
    .intro::first-line { font-variant: small-caps; font-weight: 700; color: #1d4ed8; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="demo">
    <h1>Styling the first line</h1>
    <p class="lead">::first-line styles however much text fits on line one.</p>
    <p class="intro">The first line of this paragraph is set in small capitals. Resize the window: the styling follows
    whatever text happens to sit on the first line, without any extra markup.</p>
  </main>
</body>
</html>
